🎞
"Stage Effects"/en
=== start/en
¶Press a key, click, or tap to see the same little scene six ways.

Each look is a function that gives back a list of effects. Change the numbers, or write a look of your own.¶

¶Under the sea. The deeper, the murkier.¶
ƒ underwater(depth•%) [
	Wave(0.15m · depth)
	Tint(Color(55% 45 220°) depth)
	Blur(0.03m · depth)
	Haze(depth · 60% Color(70% 30 200°))
]

¶A film a hundred years old.¶
ƒ oldFilm() [
	Grade(contrast: 130% saturation: 0%)
	Tint(Color(65% 25 70°) 40%)
	Damage(70% 50%)
	Grain(25%)
	Flicker(15% 2)
	Vignette(60%)
]

¶A television losing its signal. The weaker it is, the more static.¶
ƒ television(signal•%) [
	Grade(saturation: 140%)
	Scanlines(40% speed: 1)
	Grain((1 - signal) · 60% size: 2)
	Flicker(0.2 · (1 - signal))
]

¶A memory, soft and bright.¶
ƒ dream() [
	Blur(0.04m)
	Grade(brightness: 115% contrast: 80%)
	Haze(40% Color(95% 20 320°))
	Vignette(40% Color(95% 10 320°))
]

¶Shaking the whole stage is no effect at all: a stage can move like anything else.¶
quake: Sequence({
		0%: Pose(offset: Place(0m 0m))
		20%: Pose(offset: Place(-0.3m 0.1m) rotation: -2°)
		40%: Pose(offset: Place(0.25m -0.1m) rotation: 1.5°)
		60%: Pose(offset: Place(-0.2m 0.05m) rotation: -1°)
		80%: Pose(offset: Place(0.1m 0m))
		100%: Pose(offset: Place(0m 0m))
	} 0.6s count: 5x)

looks: ['today' 'underwater' 'old film' 'television' 'dream' 'earthquake']
turn•#: 1 … ∆ Key() | ∆ Button() … (turn < looks.length() ? turn + 1 1)

Stage(
	[
		Phrase('☀️' place: Place(1.5m 1.5m))
		Phrase('🏠' size: 2m place: Place(-1.5m -0.5m))
		Phrase('🌳' size: 2m place: Place(1.2m -0.5m))
		Phrase('🐕' place: Place(0m -1.2m))
	]
	background: Color(85% 30 230°)
	effects: turn = 2 ? underwater(70%)
		turn = 3 ? oldFilm()
		turn = 4 ? television(30%)
		turn = 5 ? dream()
		[]
	resting: turn = 6 ? quake ø
	overlay: [Phrase(looks[turn] size: 0.5m place: Place(0m -3.5m))]
)
